  "rules": {
    "summary": "30 clubs in two conferences of 15, 34 games each, 3 points a win and 1 a tie. Teams level on points are separated by total wins, goal difference, goals scored, head-to-head points and goal difference (same conference only, from 2026), fewest disciplinary points, away goal difference, away goals, home goal difference and home goals. The top nine in each conference reach the Audi MLS Cup Playoffs: 8 v 9 in a one-off Wild Card match at the 8th seed, straight to penalties if level after 90 minutes; seeds 1-7 go straight to Round One. Round One is best of three (1 v Wild Card winner, 4 v 5, 2 v 7, 3 v 6), the higher seed hosting games 1 and 3, and every level game goes straight to penalties. The Conference Semifinals (1/8/9 v 4/5 and 2/7 v 3/6, no reseeding), Conference Finals and MLS Cup are single matches with extra time and penalties, hosted by the higher seed; MLS Cup is hosted by the finalist higher in the Supporters' Shield standings. The Supporters' Shield goes to the best regular-season record.",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/2026-mls-competition-guidelines",
      "https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/major-league-soccer-announces-audi-2026-mls-cup-playoffs-schedule",
      "https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/2025-mls-competition-guidelines",
      "https://www.mlssoccer.com/standings/2026/conference",
      "https://www.mlssoccer.com/standings/2025/conference"
    ]
  },
  "notes": [
    "Playoffs: the top nine in each conference qualify. Seeds 8 and 9 meet in a Wild Card match and 1-7 go straight to a best-of-three Round One; Wild Card and Round One games that are level after 90 minutes go straight to penalties. The rest are single matches with extra time, hosted by the higher seed, and MLS Cup by the finalist with the better regular-season record.",
    "MLS's fifth tiebreaker, fewest disciplinary points, is not in the data; ESPN's published order (which matches mlssoccer.com) is used whenever its records agree with the results.",
    "Backtested on the 2024 and 2025 seasons: week-ahead match predictions score 0.224 (ranked probability score) against 0.232 for home/draw/away base rates, and playoff odds at a quarter, half and three quarters of each season were scored to set the strength drift."
  ],
